title outer loop reads the running thread (session-log baton)
prompt Keaton asked whether to pipe the last lap's JSON output into the next -p prompt via a bash variable, or to point both loops at the session-log index top rows for continuity across laps, or a better approach
think Weighed the JSON-pipe option: the loop already tees the stream to /tmp/claude_lap.jsonl, so extracting the final result event is feasible -- yet it is fragile (lap 1 has no prior; a GATES-ONLY or killed lap leaves a stale var), redundant against the curated session log we already write, and fights the launch tool's own stated design (durable memory is the repo, not a session id / tmp channel)
think The session-log index (session-logs/README.md) top rows are already a rich, ASCII, in-repo, newest-first narrative of each lap -- written every lap, never read back. Pointing the next lap at the top few rows is nearly free and cannot go stale
think The strongest form is the baton we already designed: the session log's recommend field is the explicit next-step handoff. So each lap starts by reading the top ~3 index rows AND the newest log's recommend line -- recent arc plus explicit next rung
obs Chose Option 2 refined over Option 1; declined the JSON pipe rather than adding it as augmentation, since the log's recommend line is a better handoff than the agent's raw closing text and carries none of the fragility
obs Editing launch-claude-season.rish (which only prints) and the seed does not touch a running loop -- the change is picked up on the next launch or the next pasted one-liner
file recursion-prompts/seed/autonomous-loop.seed.md added a Running thread lens (section 1) and named the recommend line as the lap-to-lap baton (section 7)
file tools/launch-claude-season.rish added the running-thread clause to both -p lines (single-lap and continuous-loop recipes)
recommend keep-going the loop now relays its own thread; next constructive rung is the Dexter cell-grid (Season G) or a cairn-first Dimeroll->Dimeroll rename
